# TypeScript Conventions

## Context

app/tsconfig.json runs `strict` with `noUncheckedIndexedAccess`, so every index access is
possibly-undefined. app/src has zero default exports and zero `any`, all 11 exported
functions declare a return type, and every relative import already ends in `.js`
(app/src/index.ts:5-8, app/src/reducer.ts:8). New code matches that baseline.

## Rule

- Export named bindings only. NEVER add `export default` to a file in app/src.
- DO NOT write `any`, `as any`, `@ts-ignore`, or `@ts-expect-error`; guard possibly-undefined index access with `?.` or an explicit check.
- Import types via `import type { ... }` (app/src/reducer.ts:8, app/src/actions.ts:7); use the inline `type` modifier only when mixing with a value import (app/src/reducer.test.ts:4).
- End every relative import with `.js` even though the source is `.ts`: `from "./types.js"`, `from "./lib/text.js"`.
- Update state immutably with spread / map / filter. NEVER push, pop, shift, unshift, splice, sort, or reverse a state array.
- NEVER assign into existing state (`state.filter = x`, `state.tasks[i].done = true`); build and return a new object instead.
- Give every exported function an explicit return type; types and interfaces PascalCase, functions camelCase.
- Name new files lowercase, hyphen-separated when multi-word (`task-list.ts`, never `taskList.ts`). Protected files: see do-not-touch.mdc.

## How to verify

1. `grep -rn 'export default' app/src` -> no output; no default export exists.
2. `grep -rnE ': any|<any>|as any|any\[\]|@ts-ignore|@ts-expect-error' app/src` -> no output.
3. `grep -rnE 'from "\.[^"]*"' app/src | grep -vE '\.js"'` -> no output; every relative specifier ends in `.js"`.
4. `grep -rnE '\.(push|pop|shift|unshift|splice|sort|reverse)\(' app/src` -> no output; no array is mutated in place.
5. `grep -rn '^export function' app/src | grep -vE '\): '` -> no output; every exported function declares a return type.
6. `find app/src -name '*[A-Z]*'` -> no output, then `cd app && npm run typecheck` -> exits 0 with no errors.
